  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "$n$ is negative **or** greater than $10,$ **and** $n$ is odd.\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $N(n):$ $n$ is negative\n\n- $G(n):$ $n$ is greater than $10,$\n\n- $O(n):$ $n$ is odd",
  "worked_solution": "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\u2227,$\" while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\u2228.$\"\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts: \n\n- **Part 1:** $n$  is negative or greater than $10.$  This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{n\\text{\u00a0is negative\u00a0}}_{\u23df}}_{N}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{\u23df}}_{\u2228}\\,{{n\\text{\u00a0is greater than\u00a0}10}_{\u23df}}_{G},\n$$\n\nthat is, $N\u2228G.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $n$ is odd. This corresponds to $O.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{n\\text{\u00a0is negative\u00a0}\\text{\u00a0or\u00a0}\\text{\u00a0greater than\u00a0}10}_{\u23df}}_{N\u2228G}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{\u23df}}_{\u2227}\\,{{n\\text{\u00a0is odd\u00a0}}_{\u23df}}_{O},\n$$\n\nthat is, $(N\u2228G)\u2227O.$",
